      "answer": "There is a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple Canadian accounts, not just MapleBridge. The affected customers are City of Verdant Bay, Maple Regional Transit Authority, MapleBay Marketplace, MapleBridge Insurance, MapleFork Franchise Systems, MaplePath Career Institute, and MapleWest Bank.\n\nThe shared failure pattern is that after migration from legacy workflow tooling to the Orchestrator product, approval workflows for region-specific (Canada) policies fail due to incorrect rule evaluation precedence. Specifically, global-default rules are overriding or bypassing country or province-specific approval rules because of issues in rule evaluation order, schema normalization mismatches, or delayed schema registry synchronization.\n\nFor example, MapleBridge Insurance experienced a timing window where some rule-evaluation pods had not yet synchronized the latest 'canada.v2' override rules and instead applied 'global.v3' rules, leading to about 117 approvals bypassing Canada-specific gating on 2026-03-12. Other customers report similar issues such as approvals stuck or auto-denied due to global-default rules evaluated before country overrides, missing audit entries, or routing to incorrect approvers.\n\nMitigations include publishing high-priority override rules to force manual approvals, adjusting rule evaluation precedence in the EN-RULES-ENGINE to prioritize region-specific rules over global defaults, and schema mapping fixes to ensure consistent key usage (e.g., 'country' vs 'country_code'). Playbooks and hotfix plans have been created for MapleBridge and MapleFork to address these issues, including manual approval channels, audit log enabling, evidence export for compliance, and rollback plans.\n\nThe root cause across accounts is a combination of migration-induced schema and rule precedence conflicts causing global default rules to override Canada-specific approval policies, indicating this is not a one-off issue limited to MapleBridge [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_e697b3abe158, art_6376b15b1c33, art_3db205cb21ca].\n\nNote that exact counts of approvals bypassed for each customer other than MapleBridge are not provided, and detailed timelines and specific patch deployment dates for all affected customers except MapleBridge and MapleFork are not fully documented. Also, there is no explicit confirmation if all seven matched accounts share the exact same failure pattern or if there are variations beyond the general precedence and schema issues described.",
